e":-0.14092209962641547,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.09596343819462383,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00017863337050531922,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":99.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.00466,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.5,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":50.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"ARKO Petroleum Corp. operates as a fuel distributor in North America. The company operates through three segments: Wholesale, Fleet Fueling, and GPMP. The Wholesale segment supplies fuel to gas stations operated by third-party dealers, sub-wholesalers, and bulk and spot purchasers. The Fleet Fueling segment engages in the operation of proprietary and third-party cardlock locations that sell fuel to light industrial trucks and commercial vehicles, and municipal entities. The GPMP segment sells and supplies fuel to ARKO retail sites. The company was incorporated in 2025 and is based in Richmond, Virginia. ARKO Petroleum Corp. is a subsidiary of Arko Convenience Stores LLC.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Arie  Kotler | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 51","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 360 people. Revenue per employee of $15.5M ranks in the top quartile among Energy peers. Each employee generates $152K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture.","financial_summary":["ARKO Petroleum Corp. is a small-cap energy business with a $625M market cap on $5.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 2% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $55M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.43\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 183% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.8316860122687277},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 14% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Energy peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ARKO Petroleum Director Andrew R. Heyer Acquires 20,000 Shares at $13.95 Each","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/arko-petroleum-director-andrew-r-heyer-acquires-20000-shares-at-1395-each","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795125046.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Arko Petroleum Corp's Dividend Analysis","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/arko-petroleum-corps-dividend-analysis-101030187.html","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1794996630.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Devon Energy Corporation $DVN Position Lifted by Ieq Capital LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/devon-energy-corporation-dvn-position-lifted-by-ieq-capital-llc.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":179517